'' WHAT A NUMERIC 'operator cast' DOES NOT REACH (structpick.tiko NumCastArgPick). In an overload
'' set an exact cast scores back exactly HALF, which fbc's hCheckCastOvlEx turns into no match: a
'' 'long' cast offered 'zstring ptr' and 'long' is 99, where tiko bound the long one. An enum
'' parameter in a set takes no UDT (99), and every converting cast shares one bottom score, so an
'' 'integer' cast offered 'long' and 'double' is 98. An enum cast into a number is 58. Before, the
'' enum lines were TKO0994, "this statement was not compiled". Lines identical to fbc-modern's.
'' TEST: cli
'' ARGS: -fmax-errors 100 --dump-ir tests/diagnostics/src/numcast-set-bad.bas
'' EXPECT-EXIT: 1
'' EXPECT-OUT: numcast-set-bad.bas(35,9): error TKO0632
'' EXPECT-OUT: numcast-set-bad.bas(36,9): error TKO0632
'' EXPECT-OUT: numcast-set-bad.bas(38,9): error TKO0660
'' EXPECT-OUT: numcast-set-bad.bas(40,5): error TKO0698
'' EXPECT-NOT: TKO0994
'' EXPECT-MAX-DIAG: 4
